## The Numbers Don't Lie

In the past year alone, there have been 781 food recalls, with Class I recalls--those posing serious health risks--making up 217 of these cases. Compare that to the total recorded recalls of 1,139, and you'll see we're hurtling toward a dubious record-breaking year. Salmonella and undeclared allergens top the list of reasons, with 200 and 311 incidents respectively.

## Repeat Offenders

It's not just the volume of recalls that raises eyebrows--95 brands have been flagged multiple times. Spring & Mulberry Inc., Moonlight Packing, and Ghirardelli Chocolate each have double-digit recalls to their name within just one year. That's not a trend; it's a pattern.

## Recent Offenses

A few shocking cases from July 15th include:

- **Adams Extract & Spice LLC**: Multiple recalls for undeclared sesame (Class I).
- **Fresh & Ready Foods LLC**: Salmonella risk due to raw chicken in supposedly ready-to-eat meals (Class I).
- **Lehi Valley Trading Co.**: Undeclared peanuts in chocolate-covered raisins (Class I).

## Questions Consumers Should Ask

If brands like Adams Extract & Spice and Fresh & Ready Foods can allow such egregious lapses, what assurances do we have about the rest of the industry? The cost of these mistakes isn't just financial--it's public trust and consumer safety.

## What Needs to Change?

From the data, it's clear stricter quality controls and better labeling practices are long overdue. The FDA's current oversight appears reactive rather than preventive. Meanwhile, consumers must stay informed and vigilant.
